# Command Index ([PROJECT_NAME])

Read when: a routine repo command is needed quickly and the current task doc does not already name it.
Skip when: the active artifact already gives the exact command to run.

Purpose: give AI agents and operators one fast command index so they do not keep rediscovering verify, package, runner, and packet commands from multiple docs.

This file is the quick index.
Deeper workflow rules still live in:

- `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md`
- `docs/PACKET_LIFECYCLE.md` or equivalent workflow docs
- `docs/DEPLOYMENT_AND_TESTING.md` or equivalent setup/runbook docs

## Most Used

| Goal | Command | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Canonical verify gate | `[VERIFY_COMMAND]` | Run before handoff |
| Sync session brief from game plan | `bash scripts/sync_session_brief.sh` | Do not hand-edit `docs/SESSION_BRIEF.md` |
| Validate orchestrator state ledger | `python3 scripts/orchestrator_state.py validate` | Packet/state health |
| Validate template placeholders and structure | `bash scripts/validate_templates.sh .` | Local template validation |
| Check template drift against source pack | `bash scripts/check_template_drift.sh . /path/to/templates-v2` | Update the source-pack path for this repo |
| Enforce same-change docs policy | `bash scripts/enforce_doc_updates.sh` | Use when behavior/commands/paths changed |
| Validate context budget | `bash scripts/validate_context_budget.sh` | Startup-context size gate |

## Runner CLI

```bash
npm run runner -- example-config
npm run runner -- config validate --project .
npm run runner -- inspect --project .
npm run runner -- plan --project . --mode orchestrator --prompt "Describe the work"
npm run runner -- graph dry-run --project . --mode orchestrator --prompt "Describe the work"
npm run runner -- packet validate --project .
```

## Packet Lifecycle

```bash
npm run runner -- packet init --project /path/to/project
npm run runner -- packet issue --project /path/to/project --title "Small bounded task" --goal "Do one clearly scoped thing" --allowed-files "src/file.ts,docs/GAME_PLAN.md" --allowed-commands "npm run check" --acceptance "change made,check passes,docs updated if needed"
npm run runner -- packet result --project /path/to/project --id P-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS --status DONE --summary "Implemented the bounded task." --changed-files "src/file.ts" --checks-run "npm run check"
npm run runner -- packet review --project /path/to/project --id P-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS --decision ACCEPT --summary "Accepted after checks passed."
npm run runner -- packet close --project /path/to/project --id P-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS --reason "Accepted and complete."
```

